# P2-D4 — Wizard orchestration I/O ports

Residual **P2-D4** keeps create/flat **orchestration hooks in the web shell**. Moving whole hooks into `@app-tour/workspace-denali` without ports would drag Next/BFF/`fetch` into the package (boundary violation).

Copy the exposure H1.c.1 pattern: **inject I/O**, keep React wiring in web.

## Tranche P2-D4.a — Flat-edit page I/O (this slice)

| Piece | Role |
| ----- | ---- |
| `OperatorFlatEditPageIo` | Shell contract: template load, tour baseline load, update tour |
| `webOperatorFlatEditPageIo` | Default BFF adapter (`/api/…` + `updateTourAction`) |
| `useOperatorFlatEditPage` | Accepts optional `io` (defaults to web adapter) |

```text
useOperatorFlatEditPage
  → io.loadWizardTemplatePayload()
  → io.loadTourBaseline({ tourId, plugin })
  → io.updateTour(tourId, payload)
  → useOperatorFlatEditPageCore (generated package chrome)
```

Hook source must not embed `/api/tours/` or `/api/settings/tour-wizard-template` string literals — those live in the web adapter.

## Non-goals

| Item | Disposition |
| ---- | ----------- |
| Moving `useOperatorFlatEditPage` / `useOperatorCreateTourWizard` into the package | Deferred — needs fuller port + chrome surface |
| Create-wizard I/O ports | **P2-D4.b** |
| Chrome React (`OperatorFlatEditPageShell`) | Stay shell UI |
| Changing package `useFlatEditPageCore` signature | Unchanged — still receives callbacks |

## Verify

```bash
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test \
  test/wizard-host-boundary.spec.ts \
  test/p2-d4-flat-edit-io.spec.ts
```

Authority: `TEMP/phases/P2-denali-extraction-plan.md` § P2-D4.a.
